{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8244660",
      "title": "Introducing the useReducer Hook",
      "sourceHash": "3baad209f9efc1b7b264f56207da978294e154ad1895545a9791652b561ce6ef",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.84,
          "end": 5.01,
          "en": "So when building more complex React apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.01,
          "end": 9.668,
          "en": "context can be a crucial feature since it can help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.668,
          "end": 14.403,
          "en": "with sharing state across multiple components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 15.51,
          "end": 18.393,
          "en": "But what about the state management itself?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 19.26,
          "end": 22.14,
          "en": "In this context, which we have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.14,
          "end": 25.77,
          "en": "we're managing this shoppingCart state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 25.77,
          "end": 27.33,
          "en": "And as you can tell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.33,
          "end": 32.33,
          "en": "these state updating functions are rather complex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.91,
          "end": 35.37,
          "en": "You could say they contain a bit more logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 38.04,
          "en": "at least a couple of lines of code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.04,
          "end": 40.92,
          "en": "And that's of course not uncommon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.92,
          "end": 44.19,
          "en": "But it also means that this component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.19,
          "end": 47.58,
          "en": "this CartContextProvider component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.58,
          "end": 49.68,
          "en": "can get a bit hard to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.68,
          "end": 52.2,
          "en": "And even more importantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.2,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "as you can see I'm always using this function form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 58.71,
          "en": "of these state updating functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.71,
          "end": 61.23,
          "en": "I'm always passing a function to them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.23,
          "end": 64.44,
          "en": "because basically almost always",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.44,
          "end": 67.95,
          "en": "if you are managing more complex state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.95,
          "end": 71.58,
          "en": "an object or an array or anything like that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.58,
          "end": 73.98,
          "en": "you will need to update your state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.98,
          "end": 77.01,
          "en": "based on the previous state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.01,
          "end": 80.553,
          "en": "So this is a pattern you'll use all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.75,
          "end": 84.27,
          "en": "And therefore it's also kind of annoying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 87.99,
          "en": "to repeat this pattern all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.99,
          "end": 90,
          "en": "And that's why in React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90,
          "end": 95,
          "en": "instead of managing state with useState and code like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.58,
          "end": 98.304,
          "en": "you could use another state management hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.304,
          "end": 102.62,
          "en": "provided by React, a hook called useReducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.93,
          "end": 108.81,
          "en": "Now what's a reducer though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.81,
          "end": 113.81,
          "en": "A reducer in React apps and JavaScript programming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.18,
          "end": 117.53999999999999,
          "en": "in general is typically a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 117.53999999999999,
          "end": 122.54,
          "en": "that reduces one or more complex values to a simpler one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 124.11,
          "end": 128.1,
          "en": "So for example, that reduces an array of numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 128.1,
          "end": 131.64,
          "en": "to a single number by adding up those numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 131.64,
          "end": 134.64,
          "en": "And it's that reducer function which you define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 134.64,
          "end": 137.133,
          "en": "that could perform these additions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 138.54,
          "end": 142.89,
          "en": "And indeed, in this demo project, which I prepared for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 142.89,
          "end": 146.07,
          "en": "you can already see a reducer function in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 146.07,
          "end": 147.963,
          "en": "in the Cart.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 149.04,
          "end": 152.57999999999998,
          "en": "Here I'm using the built-in reduce method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 152.57999999999998,
          "end": 156.03,
          "en": "that can be used on any array in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 156.03,
          "end": 158.94,
          "en": "and that's totally independent of React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 158.94,
          "end": 162.81,
          "en": "and this useReducer hook, that's really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 162.81,
          "end": 166.5,
          "en": "This method also works outside of React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 166.5,
          "end": 170.4,
          "en": "I'm using this method to define my reducer function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 170.4,
          "end": 175.17000000000002,
          "en": "that will be executed on all items in this items array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 175.17000000000002,
          "end": 179.61,
          "en": "And here I'm then basically just updating my cart total",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 179.61,
          "end": 181.77,
          "en": "based on some starting value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 181.77,
          "end": 185.52,
          "en": "by adding the price of every item times the quantity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 185.52,
          "end": 188.58,
          "en": "of that item in the cart to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 188.58,
          "end": 191.73,
          "en": "That's what I'm doing here in this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 191.73,
          "end": 195,
          "en": "And this therefore is such a reducer function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 199.41,
          "en": "because it's reducing an array of items to a single number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 199.41,
          "end": 202.653,
          "en": "the total price of all those items in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 203.91,
          "end": 207.57,
          "en": "And now the idea behind this useReducer hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 207.57,
          "end": 212.57,
          "en": "is to use that same concept of reducing one or more values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 213.48,
          "end": 218.433,
          "en": "to a typically simpler value for state management purposes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 220.44,
          "end": 223.803,
          "en": "So how do we use use reducer for state management?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 224.64,
          "end": 226.5,
          "en": "Well, in a React component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 226.5,
          "end": 230.07,
          "en": "in this case in the CartContextProvider component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 230.07,
          "end": 233.13,
          "en": "you execute the useReducer hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 233.13,
          "end": 237.063,
          "en": "just as you would execute any other React hook function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 238.71,
          "end": 242.305,
          "en": "Now the useReducer hook will then give you an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 242.305,
          "end": 245.43,
          "en": "with exactly two elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 245.43,
          "end": 248.91,
          "en": "just as useState always gives you an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 248.91,
          "end": 250.653,
          "en": "with two elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 251.82,
          "end": 255.75,
          "en": "And here in useReducer, just as with useState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 255.75,
          "end": 259.92,
          "en": "the first element you'll get back will be your state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 259.92,
          "end": 262.8,
          "en": "that's managed by useReducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 262.8,
          "end": 265.92,
          "en": "And of course we could also name this shoppingCartState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 265.92,
          "end": 267.153,
          "en": "or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 268.41,
          "end": 272.15999999999997,
          "en": "But the second value that will be part of this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 272.15999999999997,
          "end": 274.23,
          "en": "which you get back from useReducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 274.23,
          "end": 277.14,
          "en": "will now not be a state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 277.14,
          "end": 278.673,
          "en": "as you know it from useState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 279.75,
          "end": 282.7,
          "en": "but instead a dispatch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 283.65,
          "end": 288.15,
          "en": "which allows you to dispatch so-called actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 288.15,
          "end": 289.65,
          "en": "that will then be handled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 289.65,
          "end": 292.623,
          "en": "by a two be defined reducer function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 293.67,
          "end": 296.07,
          "en": "So here, I'll name it shoppingCartDispatch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 296.07,
          "end": 300.03,
          "en": "to make it very clear that it belongs to this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 300.03,
          "end": 303.753,
          "en": "But you could also just name it dispatch to type a bit less.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 305.07,
          "end": 307.17,
          "en": "But here I'll go for shoppingCartDispatch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 309.09,
          "end": 312.51,
          "en": "So now we've got the state and such a dispatch function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 312.51,
          "end": 314.16,
          "en": "but as I just mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 314.16,
          "end": 317.31,
          "en": "we now also need a reducer function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 317.31,
          "end": 321.33,
          "en": "that will actually get triggered by dispatching values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 321.33,
          "end": 324.48,
          "en": "and that will then produce a new state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 324.48,
          "end": 327.12,
          "en": "because that's the idea behind this hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 327.12,
          "end": 329.973,
          "en": "and the reducer function we have yet to add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 331.14,
          "end": 334.98,
          "en": "So therefore here outside of this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 334.98,
          "end": 336.72,
          "en": "I'll add a new function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 336.72,
          "end": 338.52,
          "en": "which I'll name shoppingCartReducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 341.37,
          "end": 345.18,
          "en": "And I'm defining this outside of this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 345.18,
          "end": 348.552,
          "en": "because this function should not be recreated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 348.552,
          "end": 351.96,
          "en": "whenever the component function executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 351.96,
          "end": 354.99,
          "en": "because it also won't need direct access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 354.99,
          "end": 359.613,
          "en": "to any value defined or updated in the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 360.45,
          "end": 364.5,
          "en": "It won't need access to props or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 364.5,
          "end": 368.193,
          "en": "Hence I'm defining it outside of this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 369.12,
          "end": 374.12,
          "en": "And this reducer function should now accept two parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 375.27,
          "end": 379.593,
          "en": "a state parameter and an action parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 381.03,
          "end": 384.54,
          "en": "And you should accept these two parameters here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 384.54,
          "end": 388.95,
          "en": "because this reducer function ultimately will be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 388.95,
          "end": 393.36,
          "en": "by React after you dispatched a so-called action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 393.36,
          "end": 396.39300000000003,
          "en": "which will also show you in a couple of minutes of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 397.40999999999997,
          "end": 400.38,
          "en": "And the action you will then dispatch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 400.38,
          "end": 402.51,
          "en": "with this dispatch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 402.51,
          "end": 405.72,
          "en": "will indeed be the action you'll receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 405.72,
          "end": 407.31,
          "en": "on that second parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 407.31,
          "end": 409.623,
          "en": "But again, you'll see that in action soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 410.67,
          "end": 413.97,
          "en": "Now the state you'll get here , on the other hand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 413.97,
          "end": 418.26,
          "en": "will be the guaranteed latest state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 418.26,
          "end": 421.34,
          "en": "of that state that is managed by useReducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 422.85,
          "end": 426.93,
          "en": "So just as you get that guaranteed latest state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 426.93,
          "end": 430.2,
          "en": "when using that function form here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 430.2,
          "end": 431.7,
          "en": "for updating the state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 431.7,
          "end": 435.36,
          "en": "React, which we'll call this reducer function for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 435.36,
          "end": 438.75,
          "en": "will make sure that you'll get the latest state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 438.75,
          "end": 440.373,
          "en": "as this first argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 442.35,
          "end": 445.71,
          "en": "Now inside of that shoppingCartReducer function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 445.71,
          "end": 448.683,
          "en": "you should then return the updated state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 449.52,
          "end": 452.82,
          "en": "And for the moment, I'll just return the unchanged state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 452.82,
          "end": 454.77,
          "en": "by just returning state like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 454.77,
          "end": 457.14300000000003,
          "en": "though that will of course soon change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 458.76,
          "end": 461.22,
          "en": "But now with that, we have a basic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 461.22,
          "end": 465.45,
          "en": "not too helpful at the moment reducer function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 465.45,
          "end": 470.28,
          "en": "As a next step, we have to connect this reducer function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 470.28,
          "end": 472.263,
          "en": "to the useReducer hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 473.46,
          "end": 476.73,
          "en": "And to achieve this, you pass a pointer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 476.73,
          "end": 481.73,
          "en": "at that reducer function as a first argument to useReducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 484.11,
          "end": 488.07,
          "en": "Now this reducer function is registered for React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 488.07,
          "end": 490.923,
